# Kaspa terminology (never get this wrong)

Kaspa is **not** a blockchain. It is a **BlockDAG** (block Directed Acyclic Graph) cryptocurrency network.

## Required language

- Call Kaspa a **BlockDAG**, a **cryptocurrency network**, or the **Kaspa network**.
- Native coin: **KAS**.
- Kasparex builds products **on Kaspa** (L1 BlockDAG + optional L2s such as Kasplex / Igra).
- Consensus uses **GHOSTDAG** (and related PHANTOM-family ideas): parallel blocks can coexist and be ordered, instead of a single linear chain that orphans competing blocks.
- That design is why Kaspa can sustain high block rates with fast confirmations while remaining proof-of-work and decentralized.

## Forbidden language

- Never call Kaspa a **blockchain**.
- Never write “Kaspa blockchain”, “on the Kaspa blockchain”, or “blockchain application” when referring to Kaspa L1.
- Do not equate Kaspa with “Bitcoin/Ethereum but faster” without stating the BlockDAG difference.
- Prefer **on-chain / network / Kaspa L1 / Layer 2** over the word blockchain when discussing Kasparex actions.

## When comparing to other networks

It is fine to say Kaspa is a cryptocurrency network **in the same category as** Bitcoin or Ethereum (digital money / decentralized ledger). Always add that its data structure is a **BlockDAG**, not a linear chain.

## Tone for Hub / onboarding copy

Explain clearly for newcomers without sounding condescending. Prefer tight paragraphs over many one-line breaks. Be accurate first; marketing second.
